Fix NULL pointer dereference segfault on every immediate poweroff/reboot/halt.

execute_shutdown_or_sleep() only assigns m->delayed_action under the
disabled (#if 0) systemd-compatible code path. elogind's actual active
path never sets it, so the forked "e-poweroff"/"e-reboot" child in
elogind_execute_shutdown_or_sleep() dereferences a NULL m->delayed_action
when logging completion, crashing with SIGSEGV right after every
immediate shutdown/reboot/halt (the action itself already completed by
then, so it's silent-but-noisy). Use the function's own action parameter
'a' instead, which is always valid.

See: https://github.com/elogind/elogind/issues/341

--- a/src/login/logind-dbus.c
+++ b/src/login/logind-dbus.c
@@ -1805,7 +1805,7 @@ static int elogind_execute_shutdown_or_sleep(
 
         log_debug_elogind("Exiting from %s", program_invocation_short_name);
 
-        log_info("Operation '%s' finished.", handle_action_to_string(m->delayed_action->handle));
+        log_info("Operation '%s' finished.", handle_action_to_string(a->handle));
 
         m->action_job = mfree(m->action_job);
         m->delayed_action = NULL;
